  "finalText": "I fixed all three regressions with small edits in `src/`. The full test suite now passes (44 of 44), and the mixed feed imports all four invoices with no diagnostics.\n\n**Changes:**\n- **Last invoice dropped (`src/csv.mjs`):** reaching the end of the file now completes a record that has started, including one ending in a quoted field or an empty field. If the file already ends with a newline, no extra empty record is added, and an empty file still gives `[]`.\n- **Half-cent rounding (`src/money.mjs`):** `parseMoney` no longer uses floating-point maths. It converts the amount to exact whole numbers and rounds half away from zero, the same way for invoices and credits. The format check (up to four decimal places) and the safe-integer limit are kept.\n- **Shared invoice numbers (`src/dedupe.mjs`):** `invoiceKey` now identifies an invoice by vendor plus invoice number. It encodes both together so different ID pairs can't produce the same key (for example `a:b`/`c` versus `a`/`b:c`). Payment routing uses the same `invoiceKey`, so payments go to the right supplier's invoice without a separate change. Exact repeats within one vendor still collapse, and conflicts still keep the first row and are reported.\n\n**Commands run:**\n1. `node --test test/*.test.mjs` before the fix: 38 passed, 6 failed. The failures covered the end-of-file record, half-cent rounding, vendor-scoped identity, the mixed feed, the shared-invoice payments and the CLI exit status.\n2. `node --test test/*.test.mjs` after the fix: 44 of 44 passed.\n3. `node bin/ledger.mjs import data/invoices.csv --payments data/payments.csv --as-of 2026-03-01 --format json`:\n   - 4 rows read and 4 accepted, with no conflicts and no diagnostics.\n   - The USD total is 1208 cents. The amounts are 1.01, 10.08, -1.01 and 2.00, and the source rows (2–5) are kept.\n   - 3 payments were applied and none were left unapplied.\n   - Outstanding by vendor: vendor-a −0.50, vendor-b 5.08, vendor-c 0.00.\n\n**Note on vendor-a:** its −0.50 balance is expected, not a new error. Its invoice and credit note cancel out, so the 0.50 payment shows up as an overpayment. Status handling and explicit payment allocation work as before.",
